Subject: [PATCH 03/12] fix(auth): validate Steam OpenID responses before login
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

steamCallback trusted openid.claimed_id from the query string without proving
the response came from Steam, so anyone could forge a claimed_id and log in as
any Steam user (authentication bypass, high).

- Added server/src/utils/oauth.ts verifySteamOpenIdResponse(): requires
  openid.mode=id_res, a steamcommunity.com claimed_id, a return_to that
  matches our own callback exactly, and a check_authentication round trip to
  Steam returning is_valid:true. Fails closed on any anomaly.
- steamCallback now verifies before creating/logging into any account.
- steamRedirect now builds its callback URL from config.apiUrl instead of the
  Host header (the callback verification requires the two to agree).
- Added API_URL to server config and .env.template.

Tests: server/src/utils/oauth.test.ts - accepts a valid response; rejects
is_valid:false, non-id_res mode, non-Steam claimed_id, mismatched return_to,
and network failures.

Run: cd server && npx jest src/utils/oauth.test.ts

